{
  "id": "jh-documents-api",
  "name": "Documents API",
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "f68a0545-5b1c-59cd-a82a-170cfa390f62",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -120,
        -140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Start\nTwo endpoints for the user's ONE base CV and ONE base cover letter. Every webhook allows only the web app's origins.\n- **GET /webhook/api/documents** (row 1) lists them.\n- **POST /webhook/api/documents/upload?kind=cv|cover_letter** (row 2) uploads a file; it REPLACES the current document of that kind (the same operation fills an empty slot).\n\nThere is no delete: a document can only be replaced.\n\nThe upload refuses requests without `X-JobHunter: 1` (`403`). CORS blocks reading an answer, not sending a plain cross-site POST, and an upload replaces the user's document and starts a paid analysis.\n\nOnly the worker touches the stored files (`WORKER_URL`, its own storage); this workflow never reads or writes them itself.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bbe5014d-8029-5da2-ab1c-fa04cb66e67e",
      "name": "GET api/documents",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "GET",
        "path": "api/documents",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {
          "allowedOrigins": "http://localhost:8080,http://localhost:5173"
        }
      },
      "webhookId": "6d1e7a42-0c5b-4e61-9a30-2b1f8c4d7e01"
    },
    {
      "id": "659f47bf-9b72-580f-a2c1-ebea3e1b2f3d",
      "name": "Sticky Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        480,
        -140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. List documents\nOne query returns **one row**: `cv` and `coverLetter` are the ACTIVE documents (the uploaded CV and cover letter, see *Base documents sync*), or `null` when that slot is empty. Replaced documents are not listed. `BaseDocumentSummary` = id, kind, sourceRef, analysisStatus, analysisError, warnings, updatedAt. Aggregated in SQL so an empty table still answers `{ cv: null, coverLetter: null }`.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b635f88f-9bed-5c13-a7cf-ac84d313c593",
      "name": "List documents",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.8,
      "position": [
        560,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "-- Parameters: [1] owner\n-- Note: never write a dollar sign followed by a digit in SQL comments. The parameters are\n-- substituted everywhere in the text, comments included, which breaks the query.\nwith docs as (\n  select kind,\n         json_build_object(\n           'id',             id,\n           'kind',           kind,\n           'sourceRef',      source_ref,\n           'analysisStatus', analysis_status,\n           'analysisError',  analysis_error,\n           'warnings',       warnings,\n           'updatedAt',      to_char(updated_at at time zone 'UTC', 'YYYY-MM-DD\"T\"HH24:MI:SS.MS\"Z\"')\n         ) as j\n  from base_documents\n  where owner_id = $1 and active and not source_removed\n)\nselect\n  (select j from docs where kind = 'cv' limit 1) as cv,\n  (select j from docs where kind = 'cover_letter' limit 1) as \"coverLetter\";",
        "options": {
          "queryReplacement": "={{ [ '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001' ] }}"
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "postgres": {
          "id": "jh-postgres",
          "name": "JobHunter Postgres"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "66ea21cf-588d-500e-ae9d-5a2523f52b97",
      "name": "Respond with documents",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        820,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 200
        },
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { cv: $json.cv, coverLetter: $json.coverLetter } }}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3f1be7ab-2111-5dcb-88e4-d89a9e3eab96",
      "name": "Sticky Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -120,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Upload = replace\n**Has X-JobHunter header?** else `403 missing_jobhunter_header`, nothing runs.\n**Check upload**: `kind` must be `cv` or `cover_letter` and a multipart field `file` must be present, at most 5 MB (checked here before anything is forwarded; the worker enforces 5 MB too) -> else `400` / `413`. The worker does the file-name, extension and content checks.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 980,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b448113c-da89-5e56-a305-2c519c3d5883",
      "name": "POST api/documents/upload",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "api/documents/upload",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {
          "allowedOrigins": "http://localhost:8080,http://localhost:5173"
        }
      },
      "webhookId": "6d1e7a42-0c5b-4e61-9a30-2b1f8c4d7e02"
    },
    {
      "id": "7cbf2665-d714-57bb-8960-3497e7bde5f4",
      "name": "Has X-JobHunter header? (upload)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        220,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "aa2d15c1-42bd-5d20-ad3d-c2b4dfce6ce0",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.headers['x-jobhunter'] }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              },
              "rightValue": "1"
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true,
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "231cc70b-ee74-5b95-9a07-00fb19a3fb44",
      "name": "Respond: missing X-JobHunter header (upload)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        220,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 403
        },
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { error: \"missing_jobhunter_header\" } }}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ddfa7db1-6e44-5d32-a57c-78902d63af2b",
      "name": "Check upload",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        440,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const item = $input.first();\nconst kind = item.json.query?.kind;\nconst fail = (status, error) => [{ json: { valid: false, status, error } }];\nif (kind !== 'cv' && kind !== 'cover_letter') return fail(400, 'bad_kind');\nif (!item.binary?.file) return fail(400, 'bad_file');\nconst bytes = await this.helpers.getBinaryDataBuffer(0, 'file');\nif (bytes.length === 0) return fail(400, 'bad_file');\nif (bytes.length > 5 * 1024 * 1024) return fail(413, 'file_too_large');\nreturn [{ json: { valid: true, kind }, binary: { file: item.binary.file } }];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8745d50b-fc52-5350-a2b0-50c56be55442",
      "name": "Upload acceptable?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        660,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "566a093a-311b-5094-b243-8a12e8b5885a",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.valid }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true,
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8f0a4c78-18fd-545d-b7b0-d5199a54952e",
      "name": "Respond: bad upload",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        660,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "responseCode": "={{ $json.status }}"
        },
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { error: $json.error } }}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "249170e6-b534-549d-b6b9-676d05d0a2da",
      "name": "Sticky Note 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        860,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Store it (replaces the old one)\nThe worker stores the file as this kind's one document in a single step: it writes the new file, switches to it, then removes the previous one. If the write fails the previous document stays in place. Same name or a different name makes no difference (no `409`).\n`400 bad_file` (wrong type, not really a PDF/Word file, bad name) is passed on; any other worker failure becomes `502 upload_failed`.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9bc294da-c865-5771-b4d8-f5afa038461a",
      "name": "Write file via worker",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        880,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.WORKER_URL }}/documents/{{ $json.kind }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 8000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "fullResponse": true,
              "neverError": true,
              "responseFormat": "autodetect"
            }
          }
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "multipart-form-data",
        "bodyParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "parameterType": "formBinaryData",
              "name": "file",
              "inputDataFieldName": "file"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "88ec72de-3641-59db-b3b8-e0c39e82cac5",
      "name": "Was the file written?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        1100,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "573904e4-da99-5c8d-83b8-4ddb24f35952",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.statusCode }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "equals"
              },
              "rightValue": 201
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true,
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "78537ea2-9318-5dae-8681-2ca446ea5c0d",
      "name": "Respond: worker refused the file",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "responseCode": "={{ $json.statusCode === 400 ? 400 : 502 }}"
        },
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { error: $json.statusCode === 400 ? 'bad_file' : 'upload_failed' } }}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2f86abd8-99c9-5690-8e39-dee9745e99b5",
      "name": "Sticky Note 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1300,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Sync, then answer\n**Trigger documents sync** calls this n8n's own `POST api/documents/sync` (with the X-JobHunter header and `?retryFailedKind=<uploaded kind>`, which makes the sync analyse a failed document of that kind again even if the file is identical; only uploads send it) so the new file becomes the active document and its analysis starts; the replaced row is marked removed. It waits at most 15 seconds and carries on either way (a slow analysis keeps running; the app polls the status). Worst case per request stays under nginx's 30 s: write 8 s + sync 15 s = 23 s. Then `201 { sourceRef }`.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "430f5fdd-8f3f-51ca-b637-b9ade71b89cf",
      "name": "Trigger documents sync (upload)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1320,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=http://localhost:{{ $env.N8N_PORT || 5678 }}/webhook/api/documents/sync?retryFailedKind={{ $('Check upload').first().json.kind }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "fullResponse": true,
              "neverError": true,
              "responseFormat": "autodetect"
            }
          }
        },
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-JobHunter",
              "value": "1"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "id": "d15e3ade-fafd-5f2e-bad6-3414ae807df5",
      "name": "Respond: uploaded",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        1560,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 201
        },
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { sourceRef: $('Write file via worker').first().json.body.sourceRef } }}"
      }
    }
  ],
